    {
        "title": "Figure 8",
        "artist": "Elliott Smith",
        "discovered": 2016,
        "image": "Figure8_ElliottSmith.jpg",
        "genre": "indie pop",
        "comment": "this was the first elliott record i listened to. i heard a recording of someone playing their cover of 'everything means nothing to me' on a blur forum back in the day and even just that little piano riff was so magnetic to me. so subsequently listening to the original song blew my mind. the rest of the album, and eventually elliott's whole discography, quickly became a love affair for me from then on.<br><br>i think about getting the figure 8 band as a tattoo sometimes but im still hesitant. part of me feels like tattooing a reference on yourself is defining yourself by other people and their art, not your own essence. and that's cringe. on the other hand, maybe im letting my fear of being cringe stop me from just doing a Nice Thing I'd Like To Do. and tbh being afraid of being cringe is more cringe than actually being cringe imo"
    },
